<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Earlier this year one of the WCA Members noted that there was no available forecast that looked at the outlook for clinker demand in light of the impact of new technologies on clinker-free cements and the increasing use of supplementary cementitious materials and other clinker substitutes \(which I will collectively refer to as SCMs\) in cement. This report looks at factors that will impact demand for clinker between now and 2050 and sets out a potential range for projected demand.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The outlook for clinker demand is critical in estimating the need for Carbon Capture and Storage \(CCS\) installations. CCS projects are capital intensive and raising the money for CCS will be a significant challenge in markets with overcapacity and low prices. Having a realistic view of the likely requirements is therefore critical for policymakers and cement producers alike. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
