/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (For reasons which we will look at later in this article, these forecasts of significant growth are unlikely. Indeed, in its latest forecast the IEA is now projecting flat demand \(at 2020 levels\) until 2035 followed by a 5% decline by 2050. Our estimates of 2024 cement demand already show a reduction of 9% from 2020 and we expect a further decline of 22% 2050, resulting in a level of 3.0 billion tpa.)
/E (For reasons which we will look at later in this article, these forecasts of significant growth are unlikely. Indeed, in its latest forecast the IEA is now projecting flat demand \(at 2020 levels\) until 2035 followed by a 5% decline by 2050. Our estimates of 2024 cement demand already show a reduction of 9% from 2020 and we expect a further decline of 22% 2050, resulting in a level of 3.0 billion tpa.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
