200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In 2020 China had a cement demand of 2.4 billion tonnes representing 57% of world consumption, a ration that had remained roughly stable since 2014. This represents a per capita consumption of 1,700 kg per capita per year compared with an average of 300 kg in the rest of the world.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A comparison with other East Asian economies is instructive. In both Japan and Taiwan consumption dropped rapidly from their peaks of 700 and 1,000 kg per capita to a level of about half of this. South Korea is perhaps the closest comparison to China, with a peak of almost 1,400 kg per capita before the 1998 Asian Financial Crisis which dropped to around 850 kg per capita, a level it has maintained since. The drop in China is likely to be more pronounced \(as a percentage of peak demand\) than in South Korea for two main reasons:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
