/P 90 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Clinker production is the main source of cement industry CO2 emissions. Today, these emissions are roughly one third from burning fuel and two thirds from limestone decomposition. As the cement industry moves from coal to lower carbon fuels such as waste derived fuels and biomass, the fuel emissions per tonne of clinker will be reduced. We expect that by 2050, the industry average specific fuel emissions will have been reduced by nearly 70%.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The projected CO2 gross emissions from cement production before carbon capture are forecast to fall from 2.4 Gt in 2024 to less that 1 Gt in 2050.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
